Loom: cheaper AMDGPU u4 byte-table lookups (vector.table.lookup of a 16-entry i8 table, 3 permutes per register).
The merge selector (byte i + 4 * index bit 3) is now index >> 1 and one v_bfi_b32 over the base selector in an SGPR
instead of and + shift + or, and an index made by masking a byte vector with 15 or shifting it right by 4 is read from
that vector directly (one whole-register shift for the latter): the lookup only reads bits 0..3 of each index byte.
IQ4_XS decode loop VALU 154 -> 138 per 128 WMMA; bit-identical results; pp2048 GPU-only SQ cycles ~-0.26%
(IQ4_XS swiglu -3.6% incl. a bank reshuffle, kqg -0.6%, ffn -0.4%, kres -0.2%, kstore flat: its banks got worse).
